## Background and Motivation

This is motivated by want to enable us to show better errors when we're inferring the behavior of parameters (services vs the body). When defining the arguments of the route handler, we assume anything that isn't a service is coming from the body. We want to allow disabling that behavior so we're adding an option to do so. This option will be set for certain HTTP methods:
- MapGet
- MapDelete
- MapMethods(new []{ "options", "head", "delete", "head" }) 

## Proposed API


```diff
public sealed class RequestDelegateFactoryOptions
{
+   public bool DisableInferredBody { get; init; }
}
```

## Usage Examples

``` C#
// This will throw since Todo won't be inferred as a body
var result = RequestDelegateFactory.Create((Todo todo), new RequestDelegateFactoryOptions 
{
    DisableInferredBody = true
});
```

## Risks

Low


## Original issue:

**2. In MapActions an implicit injection of any service returns a 400 if the user forgot to register the service in the DI container. However,  an explicit use of [FromServices] returns the correct error. This is inconsistent**

``` csharp
  app.MapGet("/findUser/{id}", (int id, IUserRepository userRepo) => {
    return $"user found - {id} - {userRepo.FindUserById(id).LastName}";
  });
```

Error for explicit use of [FromServices]

```csharp
  app.MapGet("/findUser/{id}", (int id, [FromServices] IUserRepository userRepo) => {
    return $"user found - {id} - {userRepo.FindUserById(id).LastName}";
  });
```

``` csharp
  System.InvalidOperationException: No service for type 'IUserRepository' has been registered.
   at Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.ServiceProviderServiceExtensions.GetRequiredService(IServiceProvider provider, 
  Type serviceType)
....
```

